  "solution": {
    "approach": "Accept a float value and truncate/cast it to an integer.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    float f;\n    if (scanf(\"%f\", &f) == 1) {\n        printf(\"%d\\n\", (int)f);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    float f;\n    if (cin >> f) {\n        cout << (int)f << \"\\n\";\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNextDouble()) {\n            System.out.println((int)sc.nextDouble());\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    if s:\n        print(int(float(s)))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction main() {\n    const s = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim();\n    if (s.length > 0) {\n        console.log(Math.trunc(parseFloat(s)));\n    }\n}\n\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure edge case and standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "Cast the float to an integer directly, discarding fractional part as required."
  },
  "hints": [
    "Convert the float value to an integer.",
    "Casting (int) in C/C++/Java truncates the decimal portion.",
    "In Python, int(float(s)) truncates toward zero."
